 "final_passage": "On the 200 held-out Mirefield levels, Skua achieved a significantly higher success rate than Plover-PG (44.63% vs 40.50%; paired t-test, p = 0.0029, 95% CI [1.82, 6.44] percentage points). However, the difference in normalized return was not statistically significant (62.95 vs 62.04; paired t-test, p = 0.27, 95% CI [-0.84, 2.66]), and this non-significance does not establish equivalence. The reference agent with the Tally bonus scored between the two on both metrics (success 42.10%, return 62.71), but no statistical tests were reported for comparisons involving it.",
